# SSD Upgrades & Clean Windows Deployments

Worked on five older desktop towers that were either failing to boot or running extremely slowly on aging mechanical hard drives.

Process on each system:
- Verified all motherboard connections (power, data, peripherals) to confirm the board would POST
- Removed the existing HDD
- Installed a new SSD
- Wiped any existing partitions (no data backup required — systems were being rebuilt from scratch for class use)
- Created Windows 10 installation media on a USB drive
- Configured BIOS/UEFI boot order to prioritize the USB, then the new SSD
- Performed a clean Windows 10 installation onto the SSD
- Removed old user accounts and credentials
- Created a standardized local account for classroom use
- Reassembled the tower and verified it booted cleanly

Completed three systems independently and assisted two classmates with the same process on their machines. Most of the class was still working through their first system by the time these were finished and set aside.

> [!NOTE]
> **Skills applied:** hardware troubleshooting and POST verification, storage device replacement, USB boot media creation, BIOS/UEFI configuration, clean OS installation, and user account management.
